# One line ending everywhere, including in the Windows working tree.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` hands the working tree CRLF while the
# repository keeps LF, and the two tools that read those files disagree:
# `prettier --check .` reports 200+ untouched files as misformatted, while
# `git status` stays clean because it converts back on the way in. The
# pre-commit `mixed-line-ending` hook then rewrites the staged files and aborts
# the first commit of every session, so each commit has to be made twice.
#
# `eol=lf` is what stops it: it pins the checkout, not just the blob, so a fresh
# clone or worktree on Windows gets exactly what CI on Linux gets.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
*.db binary
*.session binary
